#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068491 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068717 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e107f878-5b22-54bf-90fc-b8ea8a22c77d" :knowledge-point/title "Absolute Value Inequalities Containing a Less Than (or Equal To) Symbol"}] :question/id #uuid "60c2e025-0b7e-5ac2-afec-adeb5f65eed1" :question/math-academy-id "e-14222" :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $\\left\\vert\\dfrac{x-1}{6}\\right\\vert \\leq 1$." :question/worked-solution "We convert the absolute value inequality into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value.\n\nThe inequality specifies every number\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x-1}{6}\n$$\n\nwhose distance from zero is less than or equal to $1$. This corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n-1 \\leq \\dfrac{x-1}{6} \\leq 1\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & \\le \\frac{x - 1}{6} \\le 1 \\\\ -6 & \\le x - 1 \\le 6 \\\\ -5 & \\le x \\le 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068493 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4f7e042-a8fa-50c8-a502-1397138dc380" :knowledge-point/title "Absolute Value Inequalities Containing a Greater Than (or Equal To) Symbol"}] :question/id #uuid "8497ea21-c194-5bbf-b501-a0e9749d8dc8" :question/math-academy-id "e-14227" :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $\\mid 12x - 5 \\mid \\ge 7$." :question/worked-solution "We convert the absolute value inequality into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value.\n\nThe inequality specifies every number $12x - 5$ whose distance from zero is greater than or equal to $7$. This corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n12x - 5\\begin{vmatrix}\\le - 7 & or & 12x - 5\\end{vmatrix}\\ge 7\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve each inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}12x - 5 & \\le - 7 & 12x - 5 & \\ge 7 \\\\ 12x & \\le - 2 & 12x & \\ge 12 \\\\ x & \\le - \\frac{2}{12} & x & \\ge \\frac{12}{12} \\\\ x & \\le - \\frac{1}{6} & x & \\ge 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the final solution is\n\n$$\nx\\begin{vmatrix}\\le - \\frac{1}{6} & or & x\\end{vmatrix}\\ge 1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068510 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068718 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65964b91-8f0e-5ffc-97d3-e5b87a6bade5" :knowledge-point/title "Cases Where the Coefficient in the Absolute Value Is Negative"}] :question/id #uuid "12d8aea9-62dd-5181-bd6e-54c11eba4152" :question/math-academy-id "e-14708" :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $\\vert 10 - 2x \\vert +1 < 5$." :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}10 - 2x & + 1\\end{vmatrix}< 5; \\mid 10 - 2x \\mid \\mid < 4\n$$\n\nNow, we convert the absolute value inequality into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value.\n\nThe inequality specifies every number $10-2x$ whose distance from zero is less than $4$. This corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n-4 < 10 - 2x < 4\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods. (Remember that whenever we multiply or divide by a negative number, we have to flip the inequality signs.)\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-4 < 10 - 2x & < 4 \\\\ -14 < - 2x & < - 6 \\\\ 14 > 2x & > 6 \\\\ 7 > x & > 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo make the final result easier to read, we will rewrite it so that the smaller number is on the left:\n\n$$\n3 < x < 7\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069133 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068718 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65964b91-8f0e-5ffc-97d3-e5b87a6bade5" :knowledge-point/title "Cases Where the Coefficient in the Absolute Value Is Negative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "ab4ce6ab-f572-536f-b69b-26107e70c78f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066143} {:answer-field/id #uuid "1c0a61e3-aadd-51f2-af52-df568c7fa6e5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066144} {:answer-field/id #uuid "48a7fd8b-fc8e-504d-805e-8ece07aca323" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066145}] :question/id #uuid "0ceea8c0-f989-54a6-9f70-92e530683a94" :question/math-academy-id "q-215489" :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $1 + \\mid 17 - 3h \\mid \\le 9$. {{field-1}} {{field-2}}\n$h \\le$\n{{field-3}}"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069135 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4f7e042-a8fa-50c8-a502-1397138dc380" :knowledge-point/title "Absolute Value Inequalities Containing a Greater Than (or Equal To) Symbol"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "bcca67ee-d00b-5ed9-a1a5-a17cc2e60ae9" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066149} {:answer-field/id #uuid "33b677ae-2eee-5574-a670-188edbba3875" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066150} {:answer-field/id #uuid "503e8508-9d51-5534-9ba4-e03eddaf3997" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066151}] :question/id #uuid "a92a4124-bc7c-5436-968f-ce759fb4d648" :question/math-academy-id "q-215707" :question/problem "Solve the absolute value inequality $\\mid \\frac{5 - 9a}{2} \\mid \\ge 7$.$a$\n{{field-1}} {{field-2}}\nor $a \\ge$\n{{field-3}}"}]}
